<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ m.company.name }} accounting review</title>
{% include "_styles.html.j2" %}
</head>
<body>
<div class="toolbar"><button type="button" onclick="(function(){var r=document.documentElement;var d=r.getAttribute('data-theme')==='dark'||(r.getAttribute('data-theme')===null&&matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches);r.setAttribute('data-theme',d?'light':'dark');})()">Theme</button></div>
<main>
<header>
  <div class="sub">Accounting review · {{ m.period }} (fiscal year ended {{ m.period_end }}) · based on filings available on {{ m.as_of }}</div>
  <h1>{{ m.company.name }}{% if m.company.ticker %} ({{ m.company.ticker }}){% endif %}</h1>
  <div class="muted">Industry: {{ m.company.sic_description or 'not stated' }} · Auditor: {{ m.company.auditor or 'not identified' }} · Prepared {{ m.generated }}</div>
  <p class="muted">Company type: <strong>{{ m.profile.label }}</strong> · amounts in {{ m.currency }}{% if m.profile.excluded %} · {{ m.profile.excluded }} tests do not apply to this type of company{% endif %}</p>
  <p class="muted"><strong>Caveats:</strong> {% if m.company.warnings %}{{ m.company.warnings|join(' ') }}{% else %}{{ m.none_text }}{% endif %}</p>
  <nav class="toc" aria-label="Sections"><a href="#summary">Summary</a><a href="#dashboard">Overview</a><a href="#findings">Suspicious anomalies</a>{% if m.set_aside %}<a href="#setaside">Set aside</a>{% endif %}<a href="#tests">All tests</a><a href="#text">Disclosure changes</a><a href="#method">How this review works</a><a href="#glossary">Glossary</a></nav>
</header>

<section id="summary">
<h2>Summary</h2>
<div class="card hero">
  <div>
    <div class="muted">Risk index (0-100)</div>
    <div class="index">{{ "%.0f"|format(m.risk.index) }}</div>
    <div class="band {{ m.risk.band }}"><i></i>{{ m.risk.band }}</div>
    <div class="scale" aria-hidden="true">{% for b in [25,50,75,100] %}<span class="{{ 'on' if m.risk.index >= b - 25 else '' }}"></span>{% endfor %}</div>
    <div class="muted">Low below 25 · Elevated below 50 · High below 75 · Severe 75 and above</div>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p class="lead"><strong>Matters worth following up ({{ m.findings|length }})</strong>, most important first:</p>
    {% if m.top_sentences %}<ol class="tight">{% for s in m.top_sentences %}<li>{{ s }}</li>{% endfor %}</ol>{% else %}<ul class="tight"><li>None. No test found a warning sign strong enough to report as a finding; every result is listed under <a href="#tests">All tests</a>.</li></ul>{% endif %}
    <p class="muted"><strong>Independent re-check:</strong> {% if m.findings %}every finding was re-checked against the original filings: {{ m.audit_summary.verified }} confirmed, {{ m.audit_summary.corrected }} confirmed after corrections, {{ m.audit_summary.unverified }} could not be fully confirmed and count for half.{% else %}not needed, because there are no findings.{% endif %}</p>
    <p><strong>The question that would most change this conclusion:</strong> {{ m.key_question }}</p>
    <p class="muted">The risk index summarises how many warning signs were found and how strong they are. It is a screening score, not the probability that anything is wrong. Comparison group: {{ m.peer_method }}</p>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="card tablewrap"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Key figures (as first reported)</th><th class="num">{{ m.period }}</th><th class="num">Prior year</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{% for k in m.key_numbers %}<tr><td>{{ k.label }}</td><td class="num">{{ k.value }}</td><td class="num">{{ k.prior }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="disclaimer">{{ m.disclaimer }}</p>
</section>

<section id="dashboard">
<h2>Overview</h2>
<div class="card">
  <h3>Warning-sign strength by accounting area</h3>
  <p class="muted">The strongest test result in each area, from 0 (nothing unusual) to 1 (strongest).</p>
  <div class="heat">{% for a in m.areas %}{% set lvl = 0 if a.score < 0.01 else (1 if a.score < 0.3 else (2 if a.score < 0.5 else (3 if a.score < 0.7 else (4 if a.score < 0.85 else 5)))) %}<div class="l{{ lvl }}" title="{{ a.area }}: {{ a.score }}">{{ a.area }}<b>{{ "%.2f"|format(a.score) }}</b></div>{% endfor %}</div>
</div>
<div class="card">{% if m.charts.earnings_cash %}{{ m.charts.earnings_cash|safe }}{% else %}<h3>Net income vs cash from operations</h3><p>Not shown: for this type of company, operating cash flow does not measure how much of its profit turns into cash.</p>{% endif %}<p class="muted">Over time, profits should turn into cash. A persistent gap between net income and the cash the business generates is the most common sign that profits rely heavily on estimates.</p></div>
<div class="card">{% if m.charts.scores %}{{ m.charts.scores|safe }}{% else %}<h3>Forensic scores vs peers</h3><p>Not shown: the scoring models do not apply to this type of company, or the data they need was missing.</p>{% endif %}<p class="muted">Academic scoring models that resemble the financial profile of companies later found to have misstated their results. The dashed line is each model's published warning level; the grey dots are the comparison companies. Where the company sits relative to its peers matters more than the line.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Pressures on management</h3><p class="muted">These are not warning signs in themselves, but pressure (financial strain, leadership changes) makes earnings management more likely.</p><ul class="tight">{% for p in m.pressure %}<li><strong>{{ p.name }}:</strong> {{ p.rationale }}</li>{% else %}<li>{{ m.none_text }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div>
</section>

<section id="findings">
<h2>Suspicious Accounting Anomalies</h2>
{% for f in m.findings %}
<article class="card finding" id="f-{{ f.rank }}">
  <h3>{{ f.rank }}. {{ f.title }}</h3>
  <div class="meta"><span>Strength of evidence: {{ f.strength }} ({{ "%.2f"|format(f.score) }} of 1)</span><span>Based on: {{ f.tests|join('; ') }}</span>
    <span class="audit {{ f.audit.status if f.audit else 'unverified' }}">{{ '✓' if f.audit and f.audit.status != 'unverified' else '!' }} {{ f.audit_label }}</span></div>
  <p><strong>What we found:</strong> {{ f.what_found }}</p>
  <p><strong>Why this is unusual:</strong> {{ f.why_unusual }}</p>
  <p><strong>What it could mean financially:</strong> {{ f.what_it_means }}</p>
  <p><strong>Investigation ({{ f.investigation_status }}):</strong> {{ f.investigation }}</p>
  <dl class="kv">
    <dt>Estimated effect on pre-tax profit</dt><dd>{{ f.impact_text }}{% if f.impact_basis %} <span class="muted">(how it was estimated: {{ f.impact_basis }})</span>{% endif %}</dd>
    <dt>Is it material?</dt><dd>{{ f.materiality_text }}</dd>
    <dt>Other reasons it could matter</dt><dd>{{ f.sab99_text }}</dd>
  </dl>
  {% if f.chart %}{{ f.chart|safe }}{% else %}<p class="muted">Trend chart: not applicable, because this test does not measure a ratio over time.</p>{% endif %}
  <details open><summary>What the tests found ({{ f.signals|length }})</summary>
    {% for s in f.signals %}<div class="card">
      <h3>{{ s.name }} <span class="muted">· severity {{ "%.2f"|format(s.severity) }} · {{ s.period or 'latest period' }}</span></h3>
      <p>{{ s.rationale }}</p>
      <p class="reading"><strong>What this result means:</strong> {{ s.reading }}</p>
      <dl class="kv"><dt>What the test checks</dt><dd>{{ s.what or m.none_text }}</dd><dt>Why it matters</dt><dd>{{ s.why or m.none_text }}</dd><dt>How to interpret it</dt><dd>{{ s.how_to_read or m.none_text }}</dd></dl>
    </div>{% endfor %}
  </details>
  <details><summary>Supporting evidence: reported figures ({{ f.figures|length }} of {{ f.figures_total }})</summary>
    {{ f.graph|safe }}
    <div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Figure</th><th>Source</th><th class="num">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    {% for e in f.figures %}<tr><td>{{ e.label }} <span class="muted">· {{ e.kind_label }}</span></td>
      <td>{% if e.doc_url %}<a href="{{ e.doc_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ e.source }}</a>{% else %}{{ e.source }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ e.value_fmt or '' }}</td></tr>{% else %}<tr><td colspan="3">{{ m.none_text }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
    </tbody></table></div>
  </details>
  <details><summary>Supporting evidence: quotes from the filings ({{ f.quotes|length }} of {{ f.quotes_total }})</summary>
    {% for e in f.quotes %}<blockquote>“{{ e.quote }}” <span class="muted">— {{ e.label }},</span> {% if e.doc_url %}<a href="{{ e.doc_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ e.source }}</a>{% else %}{{ e.source }}{% endif %}</blockquote>{% else %}<p>{{ m.none_text }}</p>{% endfor %}
  </details>
  <details><summary>Independent re-check ({% if f.audit %}{{ f.audit.rounds|length }} round{{ 's' if f.audit.rounds|length != 1 }}{% else %}not run{% endif %})</summary>{% if f.audit %}
    <p class="muted">A separate check re-reads every figure and quote from the original filings and recalculates the impact. Problems are corrected and re-checked, up to three rounds.</p>
    <div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Round</th><th>Check</th><th>Result</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    {% for r in f.audit.rounds %}{% for c in r.checks %}<tr><td>{{ r.round }}</td><td>{{ c.label }}</td><td><span class="pill {{ 'flagged' if c.status == 'fail' else 'normal' }}">{{ {'pass': 'passed', 'fail': 'failed', 'warn': 'note'}.get(c.status, c.status) }}</span></td><td>{{ c.detail }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
    {% for fix in r.corrections %}<tr><td>{{ r.round }}</td><td>Correction</td><td><span class="pill normal">applied</span></td><td>{{ fix }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
    </tbody></table></div>{% else %}<p>This finding was not independently re-checked.</p>{% endif %}</details>
  <details><summary>Innocent explanations to rule out</summary><ul class="tight">{% for a in f.alternatives %}<li>{{ a }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></details>
  <details open><summary>Questions to ask management or the auditors</summary><ul class="tight">{% for q in f.questions %}<li>{{ q }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></details>
</article>
{% else %}<p>No accounting anomaly met the reporting threshold.</p>
{% endfor %}
</section>

{% if m.set_aside %}<section id="setaside">
<h2>Results set aside as probable test errors</h2>
<p class="muted">{{ m.set_aside_note }}</p>
{% for s in m.set_aside %}<div class="card"><h3>{{ s.title }}{% if s.years %} <span class="muted">· {{ s.years }}</span>{% endif %}</h3><p class="muted">Based on: {{ s.tests|join('; ') }}</p><p><strong>Why it was set aside:</strong> {{ s.reason }}</p></div>{% endfor %}
</section>{% endif %}

<section id="tests">
<h2>All tests performed</h2>
<p class="muted">{{ m.statuses.ok }} tests ran; {{ m.statuses.skipped }} could not run because data was missing; {{ m.statuses['n/a'] }} do not apply to this type of company; {{ m.statuses.error }} failed. Severity runs from 0 (nothing unusual) to 1 (strongest); a result is flagged at {{ "%.1f"|format(m.flag_at) }}. "Explained" means the result was unusual but a known legitimate cause was found. "Held back" means the result or one of its inputs was physically impossible (for example a part larger than its whole), so it was not counted. Open "About this test" for what each test checks, why it matters and how to read it.</p>
{% for fam in m.families %}
<details class="card"><summary><strong>{{ fam.name }}</strong> - {{ fam.flagged }} flagged of {{ fam.ran }} that ran</summary>
<div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>Result</th><th class="num">Severity</th><th class="num">Peer percentile</th><th>What was found</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for r in fam.rows %}<tr><td>{{ r.name }}{% if r.period %}<div class="muted">{{ r.period }}</div>{% endif %}</td><td><span class="pill {{ r.status|replace('/', '') }}">{{ r.status_label }}</span></td>
<td class="num">{{ "%.2f"|format(r.severity) if r.severity is not none else '' }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.pct_peer if r.pct_peer is not none else '' }}</td><td>{{ r.detail }}
{% if r.reading and r.reading != r.detail %}<div class="reading">{{ r.reading }}</div>{% endif %}
{% if r.first %}<details class="about"><summary>About this test</summary><dl class="kv">
<dt>What it checks</dt><dd>{{ r.what or m.none_text }}</dd><dt>Why it matters</dt><dd>{{ r.why or m.none_text }}</dd><dt>How to interpret it</dt><dd>{{ r.how_to_read or m.none_text }}</dd></dl></details>{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div></details>
{% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="text">
<h2>Changes in the company's disclosures</h2>
{% for t in m.text_changes %}<div class="card"><h3>{{ t.name }}</h3><p>{{ t.rationale }}</p>{% for q in t.quotes %}<blockquote>{{ q.quote }} <a href="{{ q.doc_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ q.source }}</a></blockquote>{% endfor %}</div>{% else %}<p class="muted">The text review did not find disclosure changes worth highlighting for this period.</p>{% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="method">
<h2>How this review works</h2>
<div class="card">
<dl class="kv">
  <dt>Company</dt><dd>{{ m.company.match_note }}</dd>
  <dt>Company type</dt><dd>{{ m.profile.label }}. {{ m.profile.description }}{% for n in m.profile.notes %} {{ n }}{% endfor %}</dd>
  <dt>What was analysed</dt><dd>{{ m.analysis_type }}. The figures come from the company's filings with the US Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC).</dd>
  <dt>Point in time</dt><dd>Only filings public on or before {{ m.as_of }}, the end of the year's filing season, were used (SEC comment letters about the year's annual report, which come later, are the one exception), and the company's figures are taken as first reported, before any later corrections.</dd>
  <dt>Comparison group</dt><dd>{{ m.peer_method }}</dd>
  <dt>Legitimate causes checked</dt><dd>{% if m.explain_conditions %}{% for k, v in m.explain_conditions.items() %}{{ v }}{{ '; ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}{% else %}No acquisition, change in accounting standards or stock split was found in the year reviewed, so no results were discounted for those reasons.{% endif %}</dd>
  <dt>Data notes</dt><dd><ul class="tight">{% for n in m.notes %}<li>{{ n }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></dd>
</dl>
<details><summary>Comparison companies ({{ m.peers|length }})</summary><ul class="tight">{% for p in m.peers %}<li>{{ p.name }}</li>{% else %}<li>None: no comparable peer group could be formed.</li>{% endfor %}</ul></details>
<details><summary>Filings read</summary><ul class="tight">{% for d in m.documents %}<li><a href="{{ d.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ d.label }}</a></li>{% endfor %}</ul></details>
<p class="muted">Limitations: this review looks for unusual patterns in public filings. It cannot verify cash, assets or transactions, and segment-level figures are not used. Tests that could not run are listed with the reason.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="glossary">
<h2>Glossary</h2>
<div class="card"><dl class="glossary">{% for term, meaning in m.glossary %}<dt>{{ term }}</dt><dd>{{ meaning }}</dd>{% endfor %}</dl></div>
<p class="disclaimer">{{ m.disclaimer }}</p>
</section>
</main>
</body>
</html>
